Context & Technical Rationale:
No runner existed: package.json had only a build script, no devDependencies.
vitest 5 + typescript 5.8 + vite 8 + @types/node mirror the parent monorepo's
proven toolchain. The package name is aliased to src/index.ts in
vitest.config.mts because the tests import '@marc-r2/crdt-contracts'; standalone
there is no node_modules link and Node self-reference requires an exports field,
which we deliberately do not add (it would restrict/alter consumer subpath
resolution). pretest runs the build so require(dist) is the artifact under test
and the compat gate reads the same compiled output consumers load. The lockfile
is committed so npm ci is reproducible.

Privacy & Security Guarantees:
Dev-only toolchain; no runtime dependencies were added to the package. No
network calls, credentials or telemetry are introduced. node_modules/ and
coverage/ are gitignored so build artifacts and installed packages never enter
history.
